  "headline": "Yoga Capital of the World",
  "short_description": "Rishikesh sits where the Ganga leaves the Himalayan foothills, known for yoga ashrams, suspension bridges and white-water rafting.",
  "about": "A major centre of yoga and meditation on the banks of the Ganga, Rishikesh gained global fame partly through The Beatles' visit to the Maharishi Mahesh Yogi's ashram in 1968.\n\nLocated in the Himalayan foothills of Uttarakhand, at the point where the Ganga enters the plains.\n\nA global hub for yoga and meditation instruction, alongside a growing adventure-sports and backpacker scene.\n\nA major Hindu pilgrimage town, with the Ganga considered especially sacred at this point.",
  "history": "An ancient pilgrimage town mentioned in Hindu scripture, historically a stop for sadhus and pilgrims en route to the Char Dham shrines in the Himalayas.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Jolly Grant Airport (airport)\n- Rishikesh Railway Station (railway)\n- Rishikesh Bus Stand (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Hindi, English\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "September to April",
  "ideal_duration_text": "2–3 days",
  "nearest_airport": "Jolly Grant Airport, Dehradun (DED)",
  "nearest_railway_station": "Rishikesh Railway Station / Haridwar Junction",
